{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cfc7QyHwH6yQ1rZDgzits", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Here's a regex that matches an ISO 8601 calendar date (`YYYY-MM-DD`):\n\n```regex\n\\b\\d{4}-(0[1-9]|1[0-2])-(0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])\\b\n```\n\n- `\\d{4}`: four-digit year\n- `(0[1-9]|1[0-2])`: month, 01\u201312\n- `(0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])`: day, 01\u201331\n- `\\b`: word boundaries, so it won't match inside longer digit strings\n\nIt matches `2026-10-01`. It doesn't check that the day exists in that month, so `2026-02-31` also matches. Calendar validity (leap years and so on) needs a date parser, not a regex.\n\nIf you need the whole string to be a date, for example when validating input, anchor it instead:\n\n```regex\n^\\d{4}-(0[1-9]|1[0-2])-(0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])$\n```"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 7558, "cache_read_input_tokens": 16830, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 7558}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "d32e2a02-4c72-4221-82a0-7d7d9b4c89e0", "uuid": "81412cd6-568a-4c1c-9052-ea51abb5dddd", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T20:00:21.475Z", "request_id": "req_011Cfc7Qy3Yb8EWxExQXDxxv"}
