 it won't match inside longer digit strings\n\nIt matches `2026-10-01`. It doesn't check that the day exists in that month, so `2026-02-31` also matches. Calendar validity (leap years and so on) needs a date parser, not a regex.\n\nIf you need the whole string to be a date, for example when validating input, anchor it instead:\n\n```regex\n^\\d{4}-(0[1-9]|1[0-2])-(0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])$\n```", "ttft_ms": 2608, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 2645, "uuid": "b6e9d6b9-6529-4a7d-b8a8-484c8bddfec7", "ttft_stream_ms": 579, "time_to_request_ms": 183, "first_content_frame_ms": 579, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
